Optimal Solution - XOR-based solution that finds the missing number by canceling out all existing values.
                   Since a ^ a = 0, XOR-ing the full range with the array isolates the missing value automatically.

class Solution {
    public int missingNumber(int[] nums) {
        // Variable to store XOR of all numbers
        int allXor = 0;
        // XOR all numbers from 0 to n (inclusive)
        for (int i = 0; i <= nums.length; i++) {
            allXor = allXor ^ i;
        }
        // XOR all elements present in the array
        for (int num : nums) {
            allXor = allXor ^ num;
        }
        // Remaining value is the missing number
        return allXor;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(n).
Space Complexity :- O(1).
